_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/.venv/bin/python3 -m pathfinder.ledger --root . --actor ada read --since 18'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/.venv/bin/python3 -m pathfinder.ledger --root . --actor ada read --since 18'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"latest substantive entry: 18\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/.venv/bin/python3 -m pathfinder.ledger --root . --actor ada add --kind finding --text 'The #16-17 subspace proposal needs a semantic split. In P, an object pose enters as a task-parameter frame for transforming and fusing *end-effector pose targets* (inputs/P.tex:412-480); masking prevents a robot-driven object from being treated as exogenous (inputs/P.tex:535-553). For a cube yaw goal, the same robot-driven yaw may still be indispensable as *feedback state* to a tendon-command controller. Keeping yaw in P-style pose-frame fusion is not equivalent to retaining yaw as feedback, and the causal action-response gate would label yaw endogenous rather than automatically preserve it. A viable experiment should compare (a) P-style frame mask, (b) direction-sensitive whole-frame mask, and (c) a controller that models object-yaw dynamics/feedback separately, using the same tracked cube pose and seven-channel commands. Q supplies the actuation testbed, not an existing pose-frame policy; a matched tendon policy must be built. This is an unresolved modeling question, not a claimed improvement.'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/.venv/bin/python3 -m pathfinder.ledger --root . --actor ada add --kind finding --text 'The #16-17 subspace proposal needs a semantic split. In P, an object pose enters as a task-parameter frame for transforming and fusing *end-effector pose targets* (inputs/P.tex:412-480); masking prevents a robot-driven object from being treated as exogenous (inputs/P.tex:535-553). For a cube yaw goal, the same robot-driven yaw may still be indispensable as *feedback state* to a tendon-command controller. Keeping yaw in P-style pose-frame fusion is not equivalent to retaining yaw as feedback, and the causal action-response gate would label yaw endogenous rather than automatically preserve it. A viable experiment should compare (a) P-style frame mask, (b) direction-sensitive whole-frame mask, and (c) a controller that models object-yaw dynamics/feedback separately, using the same tracked cube pose and seven-channel commands. Q supplies the actuation testbed, not an existing pose-frame policy; a matched tendon policy must be built. This is an unresolved modeling question, not a claimed improvement.'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"19\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I\u2019m adding the determinant calculation and the frame-versus-feedback distinction to my note. That keeps the ledger short while making the proposed experiment reviewable. I\u2019m using the style-gates skill for the Markdown note.\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/v/.codex/skills/style-gates/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/v/.codex/skills/style-gates/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nname: style-gates\\ndescription: >-\\n  Run and enforce lightweight style gates for Markdown, LaTeX, and PDF artifacts before Codex\\n  shares, commits, pushes, or produces .md, .tex, or .pdf files. Use when writing, editing,\\n  reviewing, generating, or pushing reports, papers, slides, documentation, markdown notes,\\n  TeX sources, or PDFs that should pass basic style and integrity checks.\\n---\\n\\n# Style Gates\\n\\n## Core Rule\\n\\nBefore finalizing, sharing, committing, or pushing any `.md`, `.tex`, or `.pdf` artifact,\\nidentify the affected files and run the gate. Fix failures before delivery. If a failure is\\nintentionally left unresolved, say exactly which gate failed and why.\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\nFrom the repository root, run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --changed\\n```\\n\\nBefore commit or push, prefer:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --staged\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py --changed --base origin/main\\n```\\n\\nFor a specific artifact:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 path/to/style-gates/scripts/style_gate.py report.md paper.tex slides.pdf\\n```\\n\\nUse `--strict-warnings` when the recipient wants warnings to block delivery.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Determine scope:\\n   - For generated files, pass the exact output paths.\\n   - For a commit, use `--staged`.\\n   - For a branch or push, use `--changed --base origin/main` or the relevant upstream base.\\n   - For an initial audit, use `--all`.\\n2. Run the gate script.\\n3. Fix all errors. Treat warnings as review prompts unless `--strict-warnings` is required.\\n4. For LaTeX and PDFs, also use project-native validation when available:\\n   - Compile `.tex` with the repo's existing command or `latexmk`/`pdflatex`.\\n   - Open or inspect generated PDFs enough to confirm they are not blank, corrupt, or stale.\\n5. Re-run the gate after edits.\\n\\n## Human Review Gates\\n\\nThe script catches mechanical issues; still review these before sharing.\\n\\nMarkdown:\\n- Clear title and section hierarchy.\\n- No unresolved placeholders, merge markers, stale TODOs, or fake links.\\n- Tables, lists, math, and fenced code render plausibly.\\n- Claims with external facts have sources or are clearly marked as assumptions.\\n\\nLaTeX:\\n- The file compiles, or the reason it was not compiled is reported.\\n- No unresolved citations/references in the build log when a PDF is produced.\\n- No obvious placeholder text, broken environments, or empty `\\\\ref{}` / `\\\\cite{}` keys.\\n- Generated PDFs correspond to the current `.tex`, not an older build artifact.\\n\\nPDF:\\n- File opens, has at least one page, and is not zero-byte/corrupt.\\n- Expected text is visible/extractable unless the PDF is intentionally image-only.\\n- No accidental blank pages, cropped content, or stale draft/watermark text.\\n\\n## Integration\\n\\nFor repo hooks, CI, and copy/paste setup, read `references/repo-integration.md`.\\nTemplates live in `assets/`.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/experiments/2026-09-25-repeat-injection/repeat/threads/Q8P8/ada/causal_frame_note.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/Users/v/Code_2026/pathfinder/experiments/2026-09-25-repeat-injection/repeat/threads/Q8P8/ada/causal_frame_note.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Users/v/.local/bin/style-ban-artifacts ada/causal_frame_note.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}", "{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -